text HTML
text "<nav class=\"navbar\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div id=\"navMenu\" class=\"navbar-menu\"> <div class=\"navbar-start\"> <a class=\"navbar-item\"> Home </a> <a class=\"navbar-item\"> Documentation </a> </div> <div class=\"navbar-end\"> <div class=\"navbar-item\"> <div class=\"buttons\"> <a class=\"button is-dark\">Github</a> <a class=\"button is-link\">Download</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </nav> <section class=\"hero is-link is-fullheight-with-navbar\"> <div class=\"hero-body\"> <p class=\"title\">Fullheight hero with navbar</p> </div> </section>"
button Copy danger
h3 "Fullheight hero in 3 parts #"
text To obtain a hero that will cover the whole height of the viewport, you can split it in 3 vertical parts:
text hero danger
text hero-head (always at the top)
text hero-body (always vertically centered)
text hero-foot (always at the bottom)
text Example
